From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: small uniform binds share another stage's copy of the same bytes (EDEN_UP_UBO_SHARE)

DRAFT, not built. Our own work (no upstream port). Gated by EDEN_UP_UBO_SHARE (exact 1), a live
switch (Id UboShare, not armed); off by default. On: a small (stream-path) uniform bind first
looks for another stage's allocation of the same range and cbuf index from this tick, newer
than its own, and binds it after a full compare with current guest memory. Inert with
EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD>=2, EDEN_UP_UBO_SNAPSHOT or EDEN_UP_UBO_AHEAD (FromSource binds are never
donors). EDEN_UP_UBO_SHARE_VERIFY=1 (boot) also checks the donor's ring copy and a plain guest
read. 10 s line while on: "EDEN_UP_UBO_SHARE: N tries, ...".

Reviewed draft from the draws job, v2: reviewer kept the slot serials only while the switch is
on (the off path bumped them at six exits) and left BindSmallUniformFromSource as in T122,
called CurrentTick() only when a newer candidate exists, and added "with its own copy current"
to the log line so a useful share can be told from a neutral one.
